  "description": "YELQOY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C98 H104 Gd11 N28 O68 1+,H1 O1 1-,3(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd5A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd7? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.673-4.019 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.85-118.23°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd11(ovpho)4(μ-CH3O)2(μ-H2O)2(μ3-OH)6(CH3OH)4(H2O)2(NO3)8](OH)·H2O·3CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
